#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdat; is a tar-based tape archiver. It is designed to work with multiple "
"archives on a single tape. &kdat; was inspired by two separate goals. The "
"first, was to provide a nice, &GUI; front-end to tar that supported the fast "
"selective extraction features of the <application>dds2tar</application> "
"program. The second goal was to answer my wife's question, <quote>How much "
"longer is it going to be backing up?!?</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Features"
msgstr "Foncions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple graphical interface to local file system and tape contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiple archives on the same physical tape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Complete index of archives and files is stored on local hard disk."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selective restore of files from an archive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backup profiles for frequently used backups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kdat;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mounting/unmounting a tape"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before a tape can be used, it must be mounted by &kdat;. There are three "
"ways to mount a tape:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Mount Tape</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101 index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guiicon>tape drive</guiicon> icon on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the tape drive tree node, and select <guimenuitem>Mount Tape</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdat; will rewind the tape, and read the header information from the tape. "
"If &kdat; does not recognize the header on the tape, you will be prompted to "
"<link linkend=\"formatting\">format</link> the tape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &kdat; recognizes the header it will look for the corresponding tape "
"index on your local disk. If the tape index cannot be found you will be "
"prompted to <link linkend=\"indexing\">recreate the index from tape</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If all goes well, the tape drive icon will change to indicate that the tape "
"has been mounted, and a message will appear in the status bar. The contents "
"of the tape can be explored under the tape drive tree node."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before ejecting a tape, you must unmount the tape. There are three ways to "
"unmount the tape:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Unmount Tape</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the tape drive tree node, and select <guimenuitem>Unmount "
"Tape</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdat; will acknowledge that the tape has been unmounted by changing the "
"tape drive icon, and displaying a message in the status bar. The tape may "
"now be safely ejected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting a tape"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before a tape can be used by &kdat;, it must be formatted by &kdat;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some types of tapes must be formatted before they can be used to store data. "
"<emphasis>This is not what &kdat; does when formatting a tape.</emphasis> If "
"your tape drive requires that the tapes be formatted before using them, then "
"they must be formatted before they can be <quote>formatted</quote> by "
"&kdat;. Typically floppy tape drives require that their media be formatted, "
"but DAT drives do not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to format a tape:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Format Tape...</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the tape drive tree node, and select <guimenuitem>Format "
"Tape...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will be prompted for a name for the tape, and the stated capacity of the "
"tape. Both of these parameters can be changed after the tape has been "
"formatted. The tape name is only used to identify the tape to the user; it "
"is not used to identify the tape index associated with the tape. Instead, a "
"unique tape identifier is automatically generated and written to the tape. "
"The stated capacity of the tape is used by &kdat; to warn the user if there "
"will not be enough space to complete a backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After entering the tape name and capacity, &kdat; will proceed to format the "
"tape. <emphasis>ALL DATA ON THE TAPE WILL BE LOST</emphasis>. Once &kdat; "
"has finished formatting the tape, the tape will be automatically mounted and "
"is ready for use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backing up files to tape"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before initiating a backup, you must select some files to archive. There are "
"three ways to select files for backup:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight a file or folder in the local file tree. Only the selected file or "
"subfolder will be archived."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight a <link linkend=\"profile\">backup profile</link> in the tree. "
"Only the files in the backup profile will be archived."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checkmark selected files in the local file tree. Only the checked files and/"
"or subfolders will be archived."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are four ways to initiate a backup:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Backup...</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</guimenu> "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guiicon>backup</guiicon> icon in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on a file or folder in the local file tree, and select "
"<guimenuitem>Backup...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on a <link linkend=\"profile\">backup profile</link>, and select "
"<guimenuitem>Backup...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the backup has been initiated, the <guilabel>Backup Options</guilabel> "
"dialog will appear. This dialog gives you a chance to review the selected "
"files, and change the backup options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After accepting the backup options, the <guilabel>Backup</guilabel> dialog "
"will appear. This dialog shows the progress of the backup including "
"throughput and time remaining."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Verifying tape files against local files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before initiating a verify, you must select some files to verify."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to select files for verification:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight a file or folder in one of the archives under the tape drive tree "
"node. Only the selected file or subfolder will be verified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checkmark selected files in one of the archives under the tape drive tree "
"node. Only the checked files and/or subfolders will be verified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three ways to initiate a verify:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Verify...</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</guimenu> "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guiicon>verify</guiicon> icon in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on a file or folder in one of the archives, and select "
"<guimenuitem>Verify...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the verify has been initiated, the <guilabel>Verify Options</guilabel> "
"dialog will appear. This dialog gives you a chance to review the selected "
"files, and change the working folder for the verification."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After accepting the verify options, the <guilabel>Verify</guilabel> dialog "
"will appear. This dialog shows the progress of the verification including "
"throughput and time remaining."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restoring files from tape"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before initiating a restore, you must select some files to restore. There "
"are two ways to select files for restoring:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight a file or folder in one of the archives under the tape drive tree "
"node. Only the selected file or subfolder will be restored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checkmark selected files in one of the archives under the tape drive tree "
"node. Only the checked files and/or subfolders will be restored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three ways to initiate a restore:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Restore...</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guiicon>restore</guiicon> icon in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on a file or folder in one of the archives, and select "
"<guimenuitem>Restore...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the restore has been initiated, the <guilabel>Restore Options</"
"guilabel> dialog will appear. This dialog gives you a chance to review the "
"selected files, and change the working folder for the restore."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After accepting the restore options, the <guilabel>Restore</guilabel> dialog "
"will appear. This dialog shows the progress of the restore including "
"throughput and time remaining."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid "Recreating an index from tape"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes it may be necessary to recreate the tape index file from the tape "
"contents. <emphasis>This process will overwrite any existing index file for "
"the tape</emphasis>. There are two way to recreate an index from tape:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Recreate Tape Index</guimenuitem> from the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the tape drive tree node, and select <guimenuitem>Recreate "
"Tape Index</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Index</guilabel> dialog will appear. This dialog shows "
"&kdat;'s progress as it creates the index file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a backup profile"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to create a backup profile:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guimenuitem>Create Backup Profile</guimenuitem> from the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the <guilabel>Backup Profiles</guilabel> tree node, and "
"select <guimenuitem>Create Backup Profile</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This should create a new backup profile using the currently checked files "
"and the default backup options. The following options can be set for the "
"backup profile:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "Archive name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid "The symbolic name for the archive. It can be changed later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current working folder to perform the backup in. The list of files to "
"backup is automatically updated to reflect the selected working folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stay on one filesystem"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each folder that is listed under <guilabel>Backup files</guilabel>, only "
"the files under that folder that are on the same file system as the folder "
"will be archived. Folders on different filesystems can be listed under "
"<guilabel>Backup files</guilabel>, and each will be treated independently of "
"the others, by tar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "&GNU; listed incremental"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Perform an incremental backup. A snapshot file is used to determine which "
"files have changed since the last incremental backup. Only the files that "
"have changed will be archived."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "Snapshot file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the file that is used to determine which files have changed "
"since the last incremental backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove snapshot file before backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remove the snapshot file before invoking <application>tar</application>. "
"This has the effect of backing up all of the files, and creating the "
"snapshot file for use next time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Files &gt;&gt;</guibutton> and <guibutton>&lt;&lt; Files</"
"guibutton> buttons were not fully implemented at the time this documentation "
"was written..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must press the <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> button to commit any changes "
"made to the backup profile."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring user preferences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User preferences can be configured by selecting <guimenuitem>Preferences...</"
"guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu. The following "
"preferences can be configured:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default tape size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "This value will be used as the default tape size when formatting a tape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tape block size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The hardware block size for the tape drive. For floppy tape drives this "
"value should be 10240 bytes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tape device"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The full path to your tape device (usually <filename>/dev/tape</filename>). "
"This path must point to the <emphasis>non-rewind</emphasis> version of your "
"tape device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tar command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid "The full path to the <command>tar</command> command on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "Load tape on mount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, before trying to mount a tape &kdat; will issue an "
"<userinput><command>mt<option>load</option></command></userinput> command to "
"the tape drive. Some drives may require this before reading and writing the "
"tape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lock tape drive on mount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, whenever a tape is mounted by &kdat;, the tape drive will be "
"asked to disable the eject button. This option may not work with all tape "
"drives."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eject tape on unmount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, whenever a tape is unmounted by &kdat;, the tape will "
"automatically be ejected from the drive. Do not use this option with floppy "
"tape drives."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variable block size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kdat; will attempt to change the hardware block size used by "
"the tape drive. Not all drives support variable block size. Whether this "
"feature is enabled or not, you must tell &kdat; the block size that your "
"tape drive uses (&ie; 10240 for ftape users)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdat; tape format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kdat; formats a tape it writes a single file at the beginning of the "
"tape. This file should only occupy a single tape block. The contents of the "
"file are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:585
#, no-c-format
msgid "(9 bytes) The string literal <literal>KDatMAGIC</literal>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "(4 bytes) The file format version number (currently 1)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid "(4 bytes) The length in bytes of the tape ID string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(n bytes) The tape ID string. The format of this string is "
"<replaceable>hostname</replaceable>:<replaceable>seconds</replaceable>, "
"where <replaceable>hostname</replaceable> is the full name of the machine "
"that the tape was formatted on and <replaceable>seconds</replaceable> is the "
"number of seconds since the epoch when the tape was formatted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tape ID is used to locate a file, with the same name, in the <filename>"
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kdat</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each of the remaining files on the tape are plain-old <application>tar</"
"application> archives. You should be able to manipulate them directly with "
"&GNU; <application>tar</application>. Even non-&GNU; <application>tar</"
"application> should work for non-incremental backups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu and Toolbar Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdat; menus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdat; has three menus: <link linkend=\"menu-file\"><guimenu>File</guimenu></"
"link>, <link linkend=\"menu-edit\"><guimenu>Edit</guimenu></link>, and <link "
"linkend=\"menu-help\"><guimenu>Help</guimenu></link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
